# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ARGUS environment variables
# Copy to .env.local for local dev, or set these in Vercel
# (Project → Settings → Environment Variables) for Preview + Production.
# Never commit real keys.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# LLM provider: "gemini" (default, free) or "anthropic"
LLM_PROVIDER=gemini

# Optional model override (defaults: gemini → gemini-2.5-flash, anthropic → claude-opus-4-8)
# LLM_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Google Gemini — free key, no card: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Anthropic — only needed if LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Langfuse observability (optional; cloud free tier or self-host).
# With both keys set, each brief is exported as one trace tree. Use the base URL
# of your Langfuse region: EU https://cloud.langfuse.com · US https://us.cloud.langfuse.com
# LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=
# LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=
# LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=https://cloud.langfuse.com

# ── Accounts & saved briefs (optional) ───────────────────────
# All optional and all-or-nothing. Without them ARGUS runs exactly as it always
# has — briefs are generated and kept in your browser's localStorage, and no
# sign-in control is rendered. Set all five to let people sign in with Google
# and have their briefs persist to their account.

# Supabase Postgres. Two forms of this URL:
#   · the app wants the TRANSACTION POOLER (port 6543) — Supabase → Project
#     Settings → Database → Connection string → Transaction pooler
#   · applying sql/*.sql wants the DIRECT connection (port 5432); the pooler
#     can't run DDL reliably
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@<host>:6543/postgres

# ── Attachment storage (optional) ────────────────────────────
# Retains the documents a rep attaches to a brief, so a saved brief's sources
# can be opened again. Independent of the database: leave these unset and
# attachments are still read to build the brief, they just aren't kept and their
# sources render as plain labels rather than links.
#
# Create a bucket in Supabase → Storage. Keep it PRIVATE — every download goes
# through a short-lived signed URL minted by /api/attachments after an ownership
# check, so a public bucket would hand out client documents to anyone with the
# object path.
#
# Objects are laid out as {userId}/{briefId}/{ref}. Deleting a brief deletes its
# folder. NOTE: deleting a *user* row cascades in Postgres without running app
# code, so it leaves objects behind — see removeUserAttachments().
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=            # Project Settings → API → service_role
# SUPABASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=attachments   # optional, defaults to "attachments"

# Signing secret for sessions. Any long random string: `openssl rand -base64 32`
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# The app's own public URL — used to build the OAuth callback.
# Local: http://localhost:3000 · Production: https://your-domain
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Google OAuth client (free): https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# → Create credentials → OAuth client ID → Web application. Add an authorised
# redirect URI of <BETTER_AUTH_URL>/api/auth/callback/google for EACH origin you
# sign in from — Google matches them exactly, so localhost and production are
# two separate entries.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Optional tool keys ───────────────────────────────────────
# Most gather tools are keyless (Wikipedia, company site, job boards,
# GDELT news, SEC EDGAR). These only enable extra tools when present.

# Finnhub — free financial-markets data: https://finnhub.io/register
# Without it, the financial-markets tool simply no-ops.
# FINNHUB_API_KEY=

# SEC EDGAR User-Agent — optional. SEC fair-access wants a contact email in the
# UA; a sensible non-personal default ships in code. Override to use your own
# contact, e.g. "ARGUS (you@example.com)".
# EDGAR_USER_AGENT=

# GitHub — optional. The GitHub tool works unauthenticated but is rate-limited to
# 60 requests/hour per IP; a token (classic or fine-grained, no scopes needed for
# public data) raises that to 5000/hour. https://github.com/settings/tokens
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
